From 3c84774ee39c6fb1ab092c1ba824f7b1467d1f10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xunflash <71567536+Xunflash@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 01:22:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: eliminate green flashes and out-of-order frames in Venus
 VA-API decode

Fixes green frame flashes, stale/out-of-order frames (jumping back to
earlier frames), and 30s sync timeouts on H.264 B-frame streams in
Chromium VA-API and mpv/FFmpeg on Qualcomm Venus stateful decoders:

- Enable decode-order zero-delay output (V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_DEC_DISPLAY_DELAY=0
  and DISPLAY_DELAY_ENABLE=1) for all decode formats (not only HEVC), so
  Venus emits frames immediately in decode order matching VA-API's DPB.
- Track decode submissions with a unique monotonic 64-bit tag
  ((decode_sequence << 8) | surface_slot) so stale/cancelled frames can
  never overwrite a recycled VA surface.
- Complete the decoded CPU-to-DMABUF copy in vaEndPicture (with a short
  non-blocking wait for invisible VP9 show_frame=0 frames) and sync
  pending decodes in vaExportSurfaceHandle / vaDeriveImage / vaGetImage.
- Initialize newly allocated NV12/P010 surfaces to true video black
  (Y=0x10, UV=0x80 / 0x1000, 0x8000) instead of all-zero (which renders
  bright green in YUV->RGB), and drop the redundant per-frame zero-fill
  before row memcpy in venus_surface_copy_from_yuv420.
- Query V4L2_CID_MIN_BUFFERS_FOR_CAPTURE (adding headroom), always
  re-queue CAPTURE buffers even when a frame callback skips/errors,
  reconfigure CAPTURE on mid-stream V4L2_EVENT_SOURCE_CHANGE, avoid
  POLLOUT busy-spinning while OUTPUT slots are still free, raise
  concurrent context/surface limits for multi-video pages, and emit
  H.264 level_idc=51 for 1080p60/4K streams.
